[45.794, "o", "  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;154mThe agent is not the platform.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[45.927, "o", "\r\n"]
[46.027, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245mAct II is what an agent does with a model and no platform: 42 ways\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.218, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245mto be plausibly, confidently wrong. The only thing that changed by\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.408, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245mAct V was the platform around it \u2014 a golden path, a provisioner set,\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.602, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245ma policy bundle, and an authorization model that treats an agent as\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.794, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245ma principal with a blast radius.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.93, "o", "\r\n"]
[47.03, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245mDORA\u2019s 2025 finding, in one line: where platform quality is low, the\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.224, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;245meffect of AI adoption on organisational performance is negligible.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.415, "o", "\r\n"]
[47.515, "o", "  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;255mAgentic platform engineering is not AI replacing platform engineers.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.709, "o", "  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;255mIt is platform engineers becoming the thing that decides whether\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.896, "o", "  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;255many of this is safe to turn on.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
